<Layout title={"From Loss-Making to EBITDA Positive in 18 Weeks"}>
<article class="detail-page"><a class="detail-back" href="/publications/">← Back to publications</a><div class="section-label">Case study</div><h1>From Loss-Making to EBITDA Positive in 18 Weeks</h1><div class="detail-content modal-body">
      <h4>The Situation</h4>
      <p>A regional logistics company operating 60 vehicles across North India had posted losses for 3 consecutive quarters. The promoters were considering shutting down. A structured diagnosis revealed three fixable root causes — none of which required capital investment.</p>
      <h4>Root Causes Identified</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Routes were on average 34% longer than optimal — no route optimisation had ever been done</li>
        <li>Fleet utilisation at 61% — poor load planning meant vehicles running partially empty</li>
        <li>Driver attrition at 48% annually — replacement and training cost was ₹80,000 per driver</li>
        <li>No performance management system — drivers had no accountability for fuel or time</li>
        <li>Billing disputes with 3 key clients causing ₹60L in delayed receivables</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="modal-kpis">
        <div class="modal-kpi"><div class="modal-kpi-val">+22%</div><div class="modal-kpi-label">EBITDA Swing</div></div>
        <div class="modal-kpi"><div class="modal-kpi-val">₹3.1Cr</div><div class="modal-kpi-label">Cost Removed</div></div>
        <div class="modal-kpi"><div class="modal-kpi-val">18 wks</div><div class="modal-kpi-label">Duration</div></div>
      </div>
      <h4>The Interventions</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Route optimisation using GPS data — reduced average route length by 28%, saving ₹1.2Cr in fuel annually</li>
        <li>Load consolidation algorithm — fleet utilisation improved from 61% to 92%</li>
        <li>Driver incentive scheme redesigned — linked 20% of variable pay to fuel efficiency and on-time delivery</li>
        <li>Attrition root cause analysis — addressed top 3 grievances; attrition fell from 48% to 22%</li>
        <li>Billing dispute resolution — standardised proof-of-delivery process eliminated disputes entirely</li>
      </ul>
      <h4>The Outcome</h4>
      <p>The business swung from a quarterly loss of ₹42L to EBITDA positive within 18 weeks. Full-year annualised cost savings of ₹3.1Cr were locked in. The promoters, who had been considering exit, instead chose to expand the fleet by 15 vehicles in the following year.</p></div><a class="btn-primary" href="/#contact">Request a Discovery Call →</a></article>
</Layout>
